          },
          "TSLA": {
            "midnight_fraction": 0.9976,
            "n_rows": 10294,
            "non_midnight_rows_2018_2023": 25
          }
        },
        "implication": "Both files, independently sourced (different publisher mix), show the same pathology for the same 3 tickers: overwhelmingly date-only timestamps. The brief's 16:00 ET same-session-vs-next-session cutoff rule, and the E_SAMEBAR_TEXT leak arm built on it, need to know whether a headline landed before or after the close -- that information does not exist in this field for ~99.7% of rows. With only ~25-31 genuinely-timestamped rows per ticker across 6 years, there is not enough real signal to run the same-bar arm as designed against the committed 3-ticker universe."
      },
